      {
         "id": "SECTION_introduction",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Introduction\n\nAddition appeared in every culture because it comes from the same human act of grouping. Different peoples wrote the result with bones, knots, dots, markers or beads, and each tool organized the count in its own way (<htcite0>; <htcite1>; <htcite2>).\n\nIn this class we present these tools according to the period in which they were made, following the explanations of the previous text, **Around the World (Counting)** (<htcite3>). We focus on how each tool records a group of ten, because that is where the carry appears.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "8fe2026a-08b0-4297-b480-cb76d11dfa0f",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "The Order of Addition",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
