      {
         "id": "SECTION_mesoamerica",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### In America: Adding with Mesoamerican Numbers\n\nIn the Mesoamerican system a dot is worth 1 and a bar is worth 5. To add, write the result with bars and dots: the bars are always horizontal and the dots sit above them. Two bars are worth 10 (<htcite0>; <htcite1>).\n\n#### The Game\n\nAdd the two numbers and represent the result with dots and bars. For example, 9 + 3 = 12 is written with two horizontal bars and two dots above them.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "68ecf470-69b8-4fcb-b5f8-36f7ee5aee66",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Mesoamerican sums",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "6c071696-8eb9-4bbe-8221-ffd71620c7e3",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Around the World (Counting)",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
