         "id": "SECTION_india",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### In Asia (India): Adding with Hindu-Arabic Numerals\n\nThe Hindu-Arabic numerals let us write the result of an addition with only ten symbols. When a sum reaches ten, the carry moves to the next place and the digit that stays is written in the current place (<htcite0>; <htcite1>; <htcite2>).\n\n#### The Game\n\nAdd the two numbers and write the result in the vertical addition. Type the digit that stays in the units column in the result row, and type 1 in the carry box above the tens column. The numerals are written horizontally from left to right, and the carry is written above the next place. For example, 9 + 3 = 12: type 2 in the units and 1 in the carry box above the tens.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "18ca9e1f-b936-447a-9bab-798159cefbb9",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Practicing addition with typed values",
                     "date_time": {
