      {
         "id": "SECTION_yupana",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### In America: Adding with the Yupana\n\nThe yupana, used together with the quipus, places seeds on a grid where each row is a place value (<htcite0>; <htcite1>). In this class we use the *\"Yupana Inka Tawa Pukllay\"* method, made and published by Dhavit Prem of the Associação Yupanki (<htcite2>; <htcite3>; <htcite4>). In this method, the first number is marked in red, the second in blue, and the result in green; when a row reaches ten, one marker moves to the row above (<htcite5>).\n\n#### The Game\n\nAdd the two numbers with the *Tawa Pukllay* method. Follow the steps below the yupana: mark the first number in red, the second in blue, and the result in green; then click the gray cell in the tens row to carry 1.",
               "source": [
                  {
