      {
         "id": "SECTION_conclusion",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Conclusion\n\nIn this class we used the same tools that humanity created to count (<htcite0>), but now to add. In every game we used the way each tool writes numbers — vertical cords, horizontal bars and marks, columns of beads — and practiced the carry and the complement of 10 again and again.\n\nThe tools change from one culture to another, but the idea is the same: when ten units are completed, they become one unit of the next order. Understanding this lets us add with bones, knots, dots, markers or beads — and also with the numerals we write on paper.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "6c071696-8eb9-4bbe-8221-ffd71620c7e3",
